{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is ~65.3% (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer; config_006), with avgpool essentially equivalent at ~65.0% (config_005). The image modality alone is weak (~32.8% multiprofile, config_011), but it remains entirely untested whether image adds complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA representation. This is the largest remaining design uncertainty. Question: config_030 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly extends the best RNA-only multiprofile setup by adding the image modality via simple concat fusion, using the same resnet50 encoder for which we already have a single-modality baseline. It isolates the fusion question: does the residual image signal contribute beyond the ~65% RNA-only ceiling? Why this is the best next experiment: it tests the highest-leverage unexplored axis (cross-modal fusion) with the strongest known RNA backbone and the simplest reasonable fusion/aggregation choices, avoiding confounds. If it exceeds 65%, we confirm multimodal fusion is productive and can then optimize fusion strategy (weighted) and image encoder (ViT-L). If it does not, we learn the image modality is not complementary under this setup and can redirect budget toward RNA-only encoder improvements (e.g., scgpt) or alternative image encoders. No other single experiment reduces as much uncertainty about the most impactful remaining design decision."
}

